course: dictionary
lesson: 8564
title: Scarf: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Take off scarves, bike helmets and anything with cords before playing on a climbing frame, because they can catch.» Taking something off and worrying about it catching tells you a scarf is something you wear.
explain: Scarf can also be a verb in informal American English. «Scarf down» means to eat very quickly. If a sentence is about someone eating fast, try the eating meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Most of the time, scarf is a noun. Clues like knit, woolly, silk and green help you picture it. «He opened one: a green scarf.» The word green tells you the colour, so you know it is a piece of cloth.
fact: A scarf is a long strip of warm cloth worn around the neck.
fact: A scarf can also be a square piece of cloth worn on the head or shoulders, like a headscarf.
fact: The plural of scarf can be scarves or scarfs.
fact: «Scarf down» is informal American and means to eat food very quickly.
fact: Long scarves can get caught in bike wheels, escalators and playground equipment, so tuck them in.
exercise: «Take off scarves, bike helmets and anything with cords before playing on a climbing frame.» Why? | Because they are too heavy to carry | Because climbing frames are painted | Because scarves only work in winter | *Because they can catch on the frame
exercise: Chloe says, «Your mum's scarf is so pretty, that colour's lush.» What is a scarf? | A part of a bike wheel | A football team | *A piece of cloth worn around the neck or head | A kind of sweet food
exercise: In American slang, what does «scarf down» mean when you talk about food? | To wash it carefully | To wear it in cold weather | *To eat it very quickly | To cook it slowly
test: Why should you tuck in a long scarf near a bike wheel? | It makes the bike go faster | It stops the scarf from getting wet | It keeps the wheel warm | *It could get caught and pull you in
test: Which word is a correct plural of scarf? | scarfers | *scarves | scarfes | scarvs
exam: Which of these can catch on climbing frames? Look at «Ropes, scarves and hoodie cords can catch on climbing frames» | Books and pencils | *Ropes, scarves and hoodie cords | Sandwiches and drinks | Cups and plates
